# from DACS-Standard #296 at 725fa78bd124a7adb65df27adee376d5d44a4bd7. Its keys are Ed25519,
# so artifacts signed with ecdsa-secp256k1 or sr1-aggregate cannot be verified under this
# profile and are not published or counted.
# This is a source pin, not a declaration of complete DACS conformance.
#
# Implemented and tested in this split:
# - BundleBinding BB-4 signature/member checks and strict SIG-6 envelope decoding:
#   test/bundle-binding-rules.test.ts and test/bundle-binding.test.ts.
# - BB-5..8 role-holder resolution, deterministic per-signer work limits and
#   indeterminate overflow/divergence: the same binding tests.
# - catalogBundleBindings and scanChain retain all supported BB-4-valid records,
#   regardless of signer. The unauthenticated bundle route pages persisted records.
#   test/catalog-binding-pagination.test.ts covers scan -> direct persistence -> HTTP.
#   Reindex/federation accumulation in this part retains every verified binding.
# - canonical.ts guards its wrappers against lone UTF-16 surrogates in keys/values;
#   SDK NFC behavior and valid pairs are pinned by test/canonical-rules.test.ts.
#   Other SDK canonicalizer callers have not all adopted this guard.
# - matchesVetRequirement: required AND, OR within oneOf groups,
#   AND across groups, exact verified primary, per-scheme claim normalization,
#   verificationRequired decision gate, unconditional freshness, and unknown
#   parameters unmatched. It requires an explicit session recipe roster and
#   pre-authenticated results; every included result needs an exact live recipe,
#   allowed method and trusted signer, including results with validUntil.
#   Every required/oneOf member must declare a boolean verificationRequired;
#   VerifyResult shape is checked even when verificationRequired is false.
#   BundleRequirement requires requirementVersion "1". Result and policy methods
#   must belong to the pinned eight-kind DACS-2 VerificationMethod registry.
#   Unversioned requirements select the latest version in the supplied roster.
#   Primary selection authenticates the exact result without overriding explicit
#   listing recipe pins. Every presentedBy requires a trusted method-specific
#   VerifyPrimaryClaimControl adapter; missing/rejecting/throwing adapters fail
#   closed. The adapter must authenticate holder linkage and session-bound control;
#   an identifier-existence result alone never establishes presenter control.
#   validUntil or exact-recipe defaultMaxAgeSec sets the authority window; wrapper
#   expiry/maxAge can only narrow it. See test/vet-claim-rules.test.ts.
# - Recipe policy and historical snapshot resolvers:
#   test/recipe-policy.test.ts and test/recipe-snapshot.test.ts.
# - authenticateAuthorityAttestation adapter boundary: missing, rejecting
#   or throwing adapters fail closed; adapters must authenticate original proof/hash
#   scope, signer and validator epoch. test/authority-attestation.test.ts uses a
#   signed fixture adapter; it is not a production method-specific verifier.
# - Session Vet admission in the current evidence graph. It resolves historical
#   IdentityBundle bytes, authenticates the session challenge, selects the session's
#   DACS_RECIPE_SNAPSHOTS roster and matches the listing requirement through
#   matchesVetRequirement. The counterparty's presentedBy needs a verified primary claim
#   under a roster recipe and EvidenceGraphDeps.verifyPrimaryClaimControl (DACS-2 §7.12).
#   Production installs neither a historical challenge resolver nor a control adapter,
#   so those sessions remain indeterminate. Fixture adapters drive
#   test/indexer-binding-rules.test.ts, test/current-indexer.test.ts and
#   test/evidence-graph-rules.test.ts; the profile limits are recorded below.
# - Native pay-dem inclusion and exact amount, operator-provisioned rail snapshots and
#   SB-1 settlement keys: test/native-payment.test.ts and test/indexer-binding-rules.test.ts.
#   One catalog-wide SB-2 ledger across sellers, applied on every catalog save, holding only
#   claims whose transfer the node confirmed: test/reputation-rules.test.ts and
#   test/legacy-deal-rules.test.ts.
# - DV-1..3 storage delivery from readable cleartext and node ACL metadata, read at the
#   evidence's signed deliverableAnchor (and through its AnchorBinding when the bundle carries one).
# - DACS-3 §8.5.2 agreement/listing conformance: currency, price, rail, deliverable,
#   pattern, role direction and commitment artifact (checks 5-6 are recorded below).
# - Buyer-published sealed-envelope procurement. The supplier's deal resolves the
#   listing from the publishing buyer's owner-bound anchors and credits the agreement
